---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../../lib/seo';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Automatic organization — Mouzi features"
  description="How Mouzi organizes files automatically: folder watching, silent and manual modes, scheduled organization and download-safe detection."
  canonical="/features/automatic-organization"
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbLd([{ name: 'Features', url: '/features' }, { name: 'Automatic organization', url: '/features/automatic-organization' }])]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16">
    <SectionHeading
      kicker="Features"
      title="Automatic organization"
      lead="Mouzi watches the folders you pick and moves new files according to your rules, the moment they are safe to move."
    />

    <img src="/screenshots/automatic-organization.png" alt="Mouzi settings showing watched folders in Silent, Manual and Paused modes" width="968" height="698" class="mt-10 w-full rounded-card border border-line" />

    <section class="prose mt-12">
      <h2>How watching works</h2>
      <p>
        Mouzi registers a file-system watcher on each folder you configure. When a new file appears, it waits out a
        short grace period, confirms the file is not locked by another process, then evaluates your rules top to
        bottom. The first matching rule decides the destination. If no rule matches, the file stays put.
      </p>

      <h2>Three modes</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Silent</strong> organizes continuously in the background. <strong>Manual</strong> waits until you click
        Organize Now, which suits people who prefer batch organization. <strong>Paused</strong> stops watching entirely. You
        switch modes from the tray menu, and you can also schedule organization at up to four fixed times per day.
      </p>

      <h2>Safe with live downloads</h2>
      <p>
        Files may appear before a browser has finished writing them. In Silent mode, Mouzi waits through a grace
        period and skips <code>.crdownload</code>, <code>.part</code>, <code>.download</code> and <code>.tmp</code>
        files. It also ignores zero-byte placeholders and, when lock checking is enabled, skips files that another
        process holds open. Manual and scheduled organization runs do not wait through the grace period.
      </p>

      <h2>History and undo</h2>
      <p>
        Each successful move is written to a local SQLite history. Open History from the main window to see what moved,
        where and which rule fired. An entry can be undone while the file still exists at the recorded destination.
        Details are in the{' '}
        <a href="/docs/getting-started">getting started guide</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-12 flex gap-3">
      <a href="/download" class="rounded-btn bg-amber px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-[#151004] hover:opacity-90">Download Mouzi</a>
      <a href="/docs/getting-started" class="rounded-btn border border-line px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-cream hover:bg-surface-2">Getting started</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
